    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field (mirroring the existing `membershipNumber`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto` and a small, self-contained `membershipTier(Owner)` default method:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean silver = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount()) && owner.getEmail() != null;\n       return silver ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe logic lives in a new cohesive unit (CC 1, no surrounding-class complexity added) rather than growing any existing method, touching just two files. `Integer.valueOf(0).equals(...)` safely handles a null `namesakeCount` (\u2192 BRONZE).",
